Namenda<sup>&#x000ae;</sup> (media release)</p></note></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-3-245"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Maidment</surname><given-names>ID</given-names></name><name><surname>Boustani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Memantine combined with an acetylcholinesterase inhibitor - hope for the future</article-title><source>Neuropsychiatric Disease and Treatment</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>5</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-3-245"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galasko</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Detailed assessment of activities of daily living in moderate to severe Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>J Int Neuropsychol Soc</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>446</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16209425</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ndt-3-245"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gauthier</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Mobius</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Effects of memantine on behavioral symptoms in Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease patients: and analysis of the Neuropsychiatric Inventory (NPI) data of two randomised, controlled studies</article-title><source>Int J Geriatr Psychiatry</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>459</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15852444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ndt-3-245"><citation citation-type=